    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removes the CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family</code> subfeatures for generic fonts, because no browser actually supports them.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The collector tests at <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/tests/css/properties/font-family\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/tests/css/properties/font-family</a> fail in Chrome 146, Firefox 149, and Safari 26.4.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29246.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4067860451\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246/hovercard?comment_id=4067872654&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29246#issuecomment-4067872654\">#29246 (comment)</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29439",
            "title": "Remove generic font-family features",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-09T12:50:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-09T12:50:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.17.10) found new features shipping in Chromium 148 beta which was released yesterday. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Canary/behind origin trials/enrollment/isolated contexts, it is not considered here.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With this PR, BCD will consider the following 8 features as shipping in Chromium 148:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.Credential.isConditionalMediationAvailable_static (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5164322780872704\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n<li>api.HTMLMediaElement.loading (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n<li>api.PaymentRequest.getSecurePaymentConfirmationCapabilities_static (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4727235745546240\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n<li>api.SharedStorage.get (removal) (<a href=\"https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/45930312b5e9c35bfc5334616153cc7c4a2e10dc\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.all.revert-rule (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146458504429568\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.image-rendering.crisp-edges (<a href=\"https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7585405\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>) (<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/dqAs7zmriQQ/m/tmK5bJ9sBQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref2</a>)</li>\n<li>css.properties.text-decoration-skip-ink.all (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5077600085082112\" rel=\"nofollow\">ref</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated in a different PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.PerformanceResourceTiming.contentType</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR misses:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The Prompt API that is also <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296\" rel=\"nofollow\">announced as shipping</a>. The spec's IDL is not part of webref / browser-specs, so I filed <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4231402437\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430\">w3c/browser-specs#2430</a>. Will see if the spec gets added or if we need manual IDL in the collector for this. I can follow up on this separately.</li>\n<li>SharedWorker and Web Serial API for Android. Will also follow up on this separately. Edit: See <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4231611415\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29435\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29435/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29435\">#29435</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-148-beta\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-148-beta</a></p>",
